lesson: 122
title: Taking away across ten
level: primary-1
stars: 0
explain: When there are not enough ones to take away, first take away down to ten, then take away the rest from the ten.
explain: 13 − 5: take 3 to get down to 10, then take the other 2: 10 − 2 = 8.
vars: a=name b=name t=thing n=11..18 k=2..9
need: n % 10 < k
need: n - k >= 2
answer: n - k
exercise: {a} had {n} {t}. {a.He} gave {k} {t} to {b}. How many {t} does {a} have left?
exercise: There were {n} {t} in a box. {k} {t} were taken out. How many {t} are still in the box?
exercise: What is {n} minus {k}?
exercise: {a} has {n} {t} and loses {k} of them. How many {t} does {a.he} have now?
exercise: {n} {t} lay on the table. {b} took {k} of them. How many {t} are on the table now?
test: Take {k} away from {n}. What is left?
test: {a} gives away {k} of {a.his} {n} {t}. How many does {a.he} keep?
test: How many {t} remain in a jar of {n} {t} after {k} are removed?
test: {a} puts {k} of {a.his} {n} {t} in a gift bag for {b}. How many {t} stay with {a}?
exercise: {a} had {n} {t} and handed {k} of them to {b}. How many {t} are left with {a}?
exercise: {n} {t} were in a box. Someone took {k} out. How many {t} remain in the box?
exercise: Subtract {k} from {n}.
exercise: {a} lost {k} of {a.his} {n} {t}. How many {t} does {a.he} still have?
exercise: What is {n.words} take away {k.words}?
exercise: There were {n} {t} on a table in a classroom in Glasgow. {b} took away {k}. How many {t} are still on the table?
exercise: {a} donated {k} {t} to a school in Nevada. Before that {a.he} had {n} {t}. How many {t} does {a.he} have now?
exercise: How many {t} are left if {a} has {n} {t} and gives away {k}?
test: {n} minus {k} equals what?
test: {a}'s jar in Brisbane held {n} {t}, and {k} were taken out. How many are remaining in the jar?
test: From {n} {t}, {b} uses {k}. How many {t} are not used?
test: {k} of the {n} {t} on {a}'s desk fell on the floor. How many {t} are still on the desk?
test: If you have {n.words} {t} and give {k.words} to a friend, how many {t} do you keep?
test: By lunch in Cardiff, {b} had shared out {k} of {b.his} {n} {t}. How many {t} did {b.he} have left?
exercise: had {n} {t}, gave {b} {k}. how many i got left
exercise: {a} had {n} {t}, lost {k+1}, no wait, {k}. how many left
exercise: {b} says {n} take {k} is {n-k+1}, that's wrong right? whats the real answer
exercise: {n} {t} on the table, the dog's {k+2} years old lol, {b} took {k}. how many on the table now
test: {n} minus {k}, go
test: jar had {n+1} {t}, no hang on, {n}. {b} took out {k}. how many left in it
test: {a} did {n} − {k} = {n+k}?? nah that's adding. what's {n} take away {k} for real
exam: It is given that {a} was in possession of {n} {t}, of which {k} were transferred to {b}. Ascertain the number of {t} remaining in the possession of {a}.
exam: Whereas a box contained {n.words} {t} and {k.words} {t} were subsequently withdrawn therefrom, determine the number of {t} remaining therein.
exam: Compute the difference obtained upon the subtraction of {k} from {n}.
exam: A quantity of {k} {t} having been removed from a collection of {n} {t}, state the number of {t} that remain.
exercise: {a} had {n} goldfish. Sadly {k} of them "went to the big pond in the sky". How many goldfish does {a} have left?
exercise: A shop had {n} workers. After the "rightsizing", {k} of them were let go. How many workers are left?
test: {k} of my {t} "fell off the back of a lorry" into {b}'s bag, the thief. had {n}. how many i got now
